## 6. v0.216.0 changes (LLVM lane, this release)

**Root-cause fix — slist_get OOB in `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo`**: `ssa_mem2reg_promote` returned a `SsaFunction` literal that omitted the `inst_lhs_vals: List<Int>` field, so the C emit of the resulting struct read uninitialized memory as a slist header. Symptom: `scripts/llvm_dump_ir.oo` (and any other script that imported `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_ir.oo` and then called `ssa_mem2reg_promote`) crashed at OOB value `8101242398333468672`. Fix: pass `inst_lhs_vals: new_lhss` through the new SsaFunction literal and build `new_lhss` in parallel with `new_ops / new_res / new_imms / new_bids`. Same shape applied to 4 SsaFunction literals in `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_opt_test.oo` (lines 26-35, 49-58, 72-81, 95-104).

**Full-opcode coverage in `std/llvm_codegen/llvm_text_emitter.oo`**: `llvm_format_inst` previously handled 7 opcodes (1-5, 11-12, 14-22) and returned `"; nop"` for everything else. v0.216.0 adds explicit formatting for all 55 opcodes (1-55): bitwise (6-10), extended integer compare (36-40), phi (13), memory (14-16, 21), control flow (17-19, 53-54), const (20, 22), print (23-24), float arithmetic (25-29), float compare (30-35), int casts (41-43), float casts (44-45), call (46), GEP (47), aggregate (48-49), bitcast (50), pointer/int casts (51-52), landingpad (55). Function signature extended from `(op, res, imm)` to `(op, res, lhs, imm)` to emit real SSA-value references via `%v<lhs>`. Single call site (`llvm_text_emitter.oo:37` in `llvm_emit_module`) updated.

**New coverage tool — `scripts/llvm_emit_opcode_smoke.oo` (55 lines)**: synthesises an SsaFunction with one instruction per opcode 1..55, calls `llvm_emit_module`, and asserts that no `"; nop"` marker appears. Prints `PASS` if all 55 opcodes formatted. This is the regression guard for the "6 nops" symptom the x86 lane reported for `println(1+2)`.

**End-to-end status**: the v0.216.0 source changes are in lane. The next clean oodac rebuild (currently blocked by C lane uncommitted work in c_emit_match_stmt.oo, c_emit_arc.oo, c_emit_ops.oo, etc.) will exercise the new code paths. `scripts/llvm_dump_ir.oo` will then be able to run end-to-end and confirm the SSA IR for `println(1+2)` is `const(1); const(2); add; println_int(3)` (4 instructions, zero nops).

**Lane discipline note**: no C, WASM, or x86 files were touched. All changes are in `std/llvm_codegen/` and `scripts/`.
